=== 4. PREDICTIVE REGRESSIONS, MEMBERSHIP HELD CONSTANT (15-min) ===
  coefficient on the lagged BOOK move, predicting the exchange's next move
                             subsample                    kalshi                polymarket
                             all steps    +0.000(z=+0.0,p=0.987)    -0.004(z=-0.1,p=0.924)
                   membership CONSTANT    +0.003(z=+0.2,p=0.849)    -0.014(z=-0.3,p=0.778)
         membership CONSTANT, final 2h    +0.063(z=+1.7,p=0.087)    +0.070(z=+2.6,p=0.008)
          membership CONSTANT, >2h out    -0.008(z=-0.4,p=0.715)    -0.027(z=-0.5,p=0.615)
                                                              --- final 2h, identified ---
                  same, date-clustered    +0.063(z=+1.6,p=0.100)    +0.070(z=+2.5,p=0.012)
     exchange quote AWAKE (moved <30m)    +0.063(z=+1.8,p=0.074)    +0.055(z=+1.2,p=0.244)
    exchange quote RESTING (frozen 30m)    +0.064(z=+1.4,p=0.157)    +0.079(z=+5.5,p=0.000)
        book move >=0.5pt (news-sized)                n=138 thin                n=138 thin
              book move <0.5pt (drift)    +0.113(z=+1.5,p=0.137)    +0.165(z=+3.0,p=0.002)

  mirror, same window — predict the BOOK: book(own):-0.196(z=-1.8)  kalshi:+0.005(z=+0.3)  polymarket:+0.047(z=+1.7)  n=3,072

  READ: smearing and composition both attenuate, so a coefficient that only
  APPEARS after cleaning is the case to take seriously. Identify it before
  reporting it as transmission: news concentrates in awake quotes and scales
  with move size. A coefficient that lives in RESTING quotes and in sub-0.5pt
  drift is a stale quote stepping toward a consensus that moved without it.

